Package: must
Title: Multiple-Stressor Interactions Under Alternative Null Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Amador Crespo", email = "pamadorc@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Detects and classifies non-additive effects of multiple stressors in
    experiments. Before any model is fitted, the design is described: missing
    treatment combinations, cells shared by several contrasts, replication
    units and repeated measures, and which interactions it identifies. A
    generalised linear mixed model is then fitted to each response, choosing
    its error distribution by convergence, simulation-based residual checks
    and AIC, and interactions are tested from its adjusted predictions
    against the simple addition, multiplicative and dominance null models,
    following the post-estimation inference framework of Madge Pimentel et al.
    (2025) <doi:10.1002/ece3.71959>, by default with a small-sample correction
    (restricted maximum likelihood and t distributions with the degrees of
    freedom of the experimental units). Combinations with only zeros are
    tested from the probability of that outcome. For three or more stressors
    the net deviation from the single-stressor effects is distinguished from
    the pure highest-order interaction. Interactions can be classified with
    the directional scheme of Piggott et al. (2015) <doi:10.1002/ece3.1465>.
